Description: unattended camera offload station for a Raspberry Pi
 Footage Offload Station turns a Raspberry Pi into an unattended offload
 station: plug in a camera (MTP/PTP, for example a GoPro) and all footage is
 copied to an adopted USB stick, verified, deleted from the camera, and the
 camera is released from USB. A web interface in English, German, French and
 Italian shows progress, history and a gallery.
 .
 WARNING: every MTP/PTP device connected to this computer is treated as a
 camera and wiped after a verified copy, phones included, without asking.
 Install this package only on a dedicated device.
 .
 The service runs as the system user footage-offload; a small root helper
 performs a fixed list of privileged actions. Samba (read-only share), NAS
 copy (rsync or SMB) and MQTT are optional.
